    "course": "misc",
    "doc_type": "journal_article",
    "title": "Not All News Is Equal: Topic- and Event-Conditional Sentiment from Finetuned LLMs for Aluminum Price Forecasting",
    "summary": "This study investigates the effectiveness of using sentiment signals derived from finetuned large language models (LLMs) to forecast aluminum prices. By integrating sentiment from English and Chinese news headlines with traditional tabular financial data, the authors demonstrate that sentiment-enhanced models significantly outperform baseline models, particularly during periods of high market volatility. The research further identifies that the predictive value of news is highly dependent on the specific topic, event type, and news source.",
